% ABSTRACT
\sectiontitle{Project Abstract (2 pts)}

\vspace{0.05cm}

\vspace{0.12cm}

\answerbox{14cm}{STUDYWISE – Study Material Organising and Smart Planning System is a C++ project that focuses on addressing the problem of students having to keep track of all their study material. Students save all their notes and resources in folders, and it becomes hard to find the material that they need. Students often find it difficult to decide which topic they should study first, especially when several exams are approaching and some parts of the syllabus still need attention. STUDYWISE is developed to help students make this decision in a more organized way.\\

In Phase III, the main focus was on completing the planned features of STUDYWISE and connecting them into a working application. The C++ backend manages subjects, topics and study materials, while the React frontend provides an interface through which users can access these features. The system uses JSON files to preserve academic records, and uploaded PDF documents are stored locally in the backend's uploads folder. The priority recommendation system was also implemented using five factors: exam urgency, remaining syllabus, academic importance, difficulty and subject workload. These factors are combined using a weighted calculation, and a custom Max Heap is used to arrange topics according to their priority scores so that topics requiring more attention appear first. Along with this, searching and sorting operations were integrated, and a DSA Visualizer was developed to demonstrate the working of algorithms such as Linear Search, Binary Search, Merge Sort and Max Heap operations.\\\\
Along with the main features, STUDYWISE uses different data structures and algorithms to manage academic records efficiently. Vectors are used to store collections of subjects and topics, while unordered maps help locate records using their unique IDs. Linear Search and Binary Search are implemented to find subjects and topics, and Merge Sort is used to arrange records based on selected fields such as name, difficulty, syllabus remaining and academic importance. The custom Max Heap organizes topics according to their calculated priority scores, helping students identify which topics need more attention. Study Material Management has also been added, allowing users to upload PDF files, link them with subjects and topics, and view or download them whenever required. To make the working of these concepts easier to understand, a DSA Visualizer demonstrates the operations of the Max Heap, Merge Sort, Linear Search, Binary Search and the weighted priority calculation. These features bring the different parts of STUDYWISE together into a single application for managing academic resources and making study decisions more organized.}

