% UPDATED APPROACH
\sectiontitle{Updated Project Approach and Architecture (2 pts)}

\vspace{0.05cm}

\answerbox{7.5cm}{The development of STUDYWISE follows a modular approach, with each module handling a specific part of the system. C++ is used for the backend, where Object-Oriented Programming concepts help organize information related to subjects, topics and study materials. Separate manager classes handle operations such as adding, updating, retrieving and deleting records. Data is stored in JSON files so that it remains available even after the application is closed. Uploaded PDF documents are kept separately in the backend's local uploads folder, while their details are maintained in the system.\\

The backend consists of SubjectManager, TopicManager and MaterialManager, which are responsible for managing  respective records. A Priority Engine calculates topic scores using exam urgency, remaining syllabus, academic importance, difficulty and subject workload. These scores are used by a custom vector-backed Max Heap to generate priority-based recommendations. Linear Search, Binary Search and Merge Sort are also implemented to support searching and sorting operations. The frontend is developed using React, Vite and Tailwind CSS, while the Crow framework connects it to the C++ backend through REST APIs. In the final development stage, a DSA Visualizer was integrated to demonstrate the working of the Max Heap, searching and sorting algorithms, and priority calculation. This modular design brings the different features together in one application while keeping their implementation and responsibilities organized.}



