% OUTCOMES
\sectiontitle{Project Outcome/Deliverables (2 pts)}

\answerbox{10.1cm}{The final outcome of STUDYWISE is a web-based study management system that helps students organize their academic subjects, topics and study materials in one place. The application combines a C++ backend with a React frontend and uses Object-Oriented Programming concepts to manage academic records. Separate manager classes handle operations such as adding, updating, retrieving and deleting records, while JSON files are used to preserve information between application sessions.\\

One of the main features is the priority-based recommendation system. It calculates a score for each eligible topic by considering five factors: exam urgency, remaining syllabus, academic importance, difficulty and subject workload. These factors are combined using a weighted calculation, and a custom vector-backed Max Heap is used to arrange topics according to their priority. This helps students identify which topics require more attention.\\

STUDYWISE also includes searching and sorting functionality using Linear Search, Binary Search and Merge Sort. The Study Material Management module allows users to upload PDF documents, associate them with subjects and topics, and view, download, replace or delete them. The uploaded files are stored locally in the backend, while their details are maintained in JSON format.\\

Another important deliverable is the DSA Visualizer, which demonstrates the working of the custom Max Heap, Merge Sort, Linear Search, Binary Search and weighted priority calculation. It helps users understand the algorithms through step-by-step visual representations. Overall, STUDYWISE brings together C++, OOP, DSA, file handling and web technologies in a single application designed to make academic resource management more organized and accessible.}

\sectiontitle{Progress Overview (2 pts)}

\vspace{5mm}

\answerbox{10cm}{During Phase III, STUDYWISE progressed from a basic working prototype to a more complete study management application. The main modules planned in the earlier phase were implemented and connected through the C++ backend and React frontend. The project continued to focus on Object-Oriented Programming and Data Structures and Algorithms, with each feature developed and integrated into the existing system.

The backend was extended to manage subjects, topics and study materials through separate manager classes. The searching and sorting functionalities were implemented using Linear Search, Binary Search and Merge Sort. The Stage 4 priority recommendation system was also completed using a weighted calculation based on exam urgency, remaining syllabus, academic importance, difficulty and subject workload. A custom vector-backed Max Heap was integrated to arrange topics according to their priority scores and generate recommendations.

A major addition in this phase was the Study Material Management module. It allows users to upload PDF documents, associate them with subjects and topics, and view, download, replace or delete them. The uploaded files are stored locally in the backend, while their details are maintained in JSON files. The final development stage introduced a DSA Visualizer with demonstrations of Max Heap operations, Merge Sort, Linear Search, Binary Search and weighted priority calculation.

The frontend and backend were integrated using the Crow framework and REST APIs. The completed application was subjected to build checks, API testing, persistence verification and regression testing to check the working of existing features. Overall, Phase III brought the major components of STUDYWISE together into a functional application, completing the planned development work and preparing the project for its final demonstration.}

