\answerbox{19cm}{The development of STUDYWISE was completed through a series of stages, with each stage adding new features to the application. During Phase III, the main focus was on completing the backend modules, integrating the frontend, implementing the required DSA algorithms and testing the overall system.\\

1.Basic C++ Models and Backend Setup (Completed):The Subject, Topic and StudyMaterial classes were implemented using OOP concepts. The backend was developed using C++ and the Crow framework, with CMake used for compilation and build configuration.\\

2.Subject and Topic Management (Completed):SubjectManager and TopicManager were implemented to handle adding, updating, retrieving and deleting records. Input validation, subject-topic relationships and JSON persistence were also incorporated.\\

3.Priority Calculation (Completed):The Priority Engine was implemented using five factors: exam urgency, remaining syllabus, academic importance, difficulty and subject workload. Weighted scores are calculated to identify topics that require more attention.\\

4.Custom Max Heap (Completed):A custom vector-backed Max Heap was implemented to organize topics according to their priority scores. It is integrated with the recommendation system to display higher-priority topics first.\\

5.Searching and Sorting (Completed):Linear Search, Binary Search and Merge Sort were implemented in C++. These algorithms support searching for subjects and topics and sorting records using different attributes.\\

6.Study Material Management and File Handling (Completed): MaterialManager was implemented to manage study material records. Users can upload PDF documents, associate them with subjects and topics, view, download, replace and delete files. Material information is stored in JSON files, while uploaded PDFs are maintained in the backend's local uploads directory.\\

7.DSA Visualization (Implemented):A DSA Visualizer was added to demonstrate Max Heap operations, Merge Sort, Linear Search, Binary Search and weighted priority calculation. The visualizer uses data and operation traces provided by the C++ backend.\\

8.Frontend Integration and Testing (Completed):The React frontend was connected to the C++ backend through REST APIs. The completed modules were built and tested, including API functionality, JSON persistence and regression checks to verify that previously implemented features continued to work.\\

Overall, the major development tasks of STUDYWISE have been implemented and integrated into a single application. The project now provides subject and topic management, priority-based recommendations, study material organization and visual demonstrations of the DSA concepts used in its backend.}

